IMPORT prelude

-- Part VII, Division 1 of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): Construction, sections 58 to 62E.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- A function answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes or no, and NOTHING where it does not.
-- Whether a construction promotes a purpose, whether material is capable of assisting, and whether a provision is ambiguous are judgments the text leaves open:
-- they are plain inputs.

§ `Sections 58 to 62: construction subject to power`

-- An Act amending another Act, or a South Australian law applied to the Territory, is construed with that other Act or law and as part of it.
-- src:725 | An Act amending another Act or a law of the State of South Australia in its application to the Territory shall be construed with that other Act or law of the State and as part thereof.
@ref s 58 (src:725)
GIVEN `the Act amends another Act or a law of the State of South Australia in its application to the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 58: the amending Act is construed with the other Act or law and as part of it` MEANS
    IF `the Act amends another Act or a law of the State of South Australia in its application to the Territory` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Every Act is read subject to the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 and other Commonwealth Acts on the Assembly's power, so as not to exceed that power;
-- where an Act would otherwise be construed as in excess of the power, it stands to the extent that it is not in excess.
-- src:727 | Every Act shall be read and construed subject to the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 of the Commonwealth and any other Act of the Commonwealth relating to the power of the Legislative Assembly to make laws in respect of particular matters, and so as not to exceed the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly, to the intent that where any Act would, but for this section, have been construed as being in excess of that power it shall nevertheless be a valid Act to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power.
@ref s 59 (src:727)
GIVEN `the Act would, but for section 59, be construed as being in excess of the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the Act asked about is within that power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59: the part of the Act stands` MEANS
    IF `the Act would, but for section 59, be construed as being in excess of the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly`
    THEN JUST `the part of the Act asked about is within that power`
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of place on Aboriginal land` IS ONE OF
    `a place that is on Aboriginal land and that, but for that fact, the reference would have included`
    `a place on Aboriginal land that the reference would not have included`
    `a place that is not on Aboriginal land`

-- A reference in a law of the Territory to a public place or like place includes, and always has included, a place that is on Aboriginal land and that the reference would otherwise have included,
-- even though the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976 of the Commonwealth or the Aboriginal Land Act 1978 limits who may enter and remain there.
-- src:729 | (1) Where by or under a law of the Territory a right, privilege, obligation or liability is expressed or implied to be acquired, accrued or incurred by reference to a public place, public street, public road, place of public resort or other place, however described, open to or used by the public or to which the public has access, whether as of right or on the payment of a fee or other charge, that reference includes, and shall be deemed always to have included, any place which but for the fact that it was on Aboriginal land within the meaning of the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976 of the Commonwealth, would have been included in such a reference, and even though that Act of the Commonwealth or the Aboriginal Land Act 1978 limits the persons or classes of persons who may enter and remain on that Aboriginal land.
@ref s 59A(1) (src:729)
GIVEN `the reference is in a law of the Territory that expresses or implies a right, privilege, obligation or liability by reference to a public place, public street, public road, place of public resort or other place open to or used by the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `Kind of place on Aboriginal land`
      `an Act limits the persons or classes of persons who may enter and remain on that Aboriginal land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59A(1): the reference includes the place` MEANS
    IF   `the reference is in a law of the Territory that expresses or implies a right, privilege, obligation or liability by reference to a public place, public street, public road, place of public resort or other place open to or used by the public`
    THEN CONSIDER place
         WHEN `a place that is on Aboriginal land and that, but for that fact, the reference would have included` THEN
             CONSIDER `an Act limits the persons or classes of persons who may enter and remain on that Aboriginal land`
             WHEN TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- For such a law, the persons who are not precluded from entering or remaining on Aboriginal land, or who are on it whether or not they are entitled to be, are capable of constituting, and always have been capable of constituting, a section of the public in relation to that land.
-- src:730 | (2) For the purposes of a law of the Territory referred to in subsection (1), the persons who are not precluded by the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976 of the Commonwealth or the Aboriginal Land Act 1978 from entering or remaining on Aboriginal land, or who are on Aboriginal land whether or not they are entitled by those Acts, or either of them, to enter or remain on Aboriginal land, are capable of constituting, and shall be deemed always to have been capable of constituting, a section of the public in relation to that land.
@ref s 59A(2) (src:730)
GIVEN `they are persons not precluded by the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976 or the Aboriginal Land Act 1978 from entering or remaining on the Aboriginal land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are on the Aboriginal land, whether or not they are entitled by those Acts to enter or remain on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59A(2): the persons are capable of constituting a section of the public in relation to the land` MEANS
    IF   `they are persons not precluded by the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976 or the Aboriginal Land Act 1978 from entering or remaining on the Aboriginal land`
         OR `they are on the Aboriginal land, whether or not they are entitled by those Acts to enter or remain on it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- A statutory instrument is read subject to the Act under which it was made and so as not to exceed the power; where it would otherwise be construed as in excess, it stands to the extent that it is not in excess.
-- src:732 | (1) If an Act confers upon any authority power to make, grant or issue a statutory instrument, any instrument so made, granted or issued shall be read and construed subject to the Act under which it was made and so as not to exceed the power of that authority, to the intent that, where any such instrument would, but for this section, have been construed as being in excess of the power conferred upon that authority, it shall nevertheless be a valid instrument to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power.
@ref s 61(1) (src:732)
GIVEN `the instrument would, but for section 61, be construed as being in excess of the power conferred upon the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the instrument asked about is within that power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(1): the part of the instrument stands` MEANS
    IF `the instrument would, but for section 61, be construed as being in excess of the power conferred upon the authority`
    THEN JUST `the part of the instrument asked about is within that power`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- It is presumed, unless the contrary is proved, that all conditions and steps required for making the statutory instrument have been satisfied and carried out.
-- src:733 | (2) It is presumed, unless the contrary is proved, that all conditions and steps required for the making, granting or issuing of a statutory instrument have been satisfied and carried out.
@ref s 61(2) (src:733)
GIVEN `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(2): the conditions and steps required for the making of the instrument are presumed to have been satisfied and carried out` MEANS
    JUST (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

-- A resolution passed by the Legislative Assembly purportedly under an Act is read subject to the Self-Government Act and the Act in question; where it would otherwise be construed as in excess of authority, it stands to the extent that it is not.
-- src:735 | Where a resolution is passed by the Legislative Assembly purportedly in pursuance of an Act, the resolution shall be read and construed subject to the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 of the Commonwealth and to the Act in pursuance of which it purports to have been passed, to the intent that, where the resolution would, but for this section, have been construed as being in excess of authority, it shall, nevertheless, be a valid resolution to the extent to which it is not in excess of authority.
@ref s 62 (src:735)
GIVEN `the resolution would, but for section 62, be construed as being in excess of authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the resolution asked about is within authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62: the part of the resolution stands` MEANS
    IF `the resolution would, but for section 62, be construed as being in excess of authority`
    THEN JUST `the part of the resolution asked about is within authority`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 62A to 62E: purpose, extrinsic material, drafting practice, examples and notes`

-- A construction that promotes the purpose or object underlying the Act is to be preferred to one that does not.
-- Where both or neither promote it, the section does not choose.
-- src:737 | In interpreting a provision of an Act, a construction that promotes the purpose or object underlying the Act (whether the purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act or not) is to be preferred to a construction that does not promote the purpose or object.
@ref s 62A (src:737)
GIVEN `the first construction promotes the purpose or object underlying the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second construction promotes the purpose or object underlying the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62A: the first construction is to be preferred to the second` MEANS
    IF   `the first construction promotes the purpose or object underlying the Act` AND (NOT `the second construction promotes the purpose or object underlying the Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF   (NOT `the first construction promotes the purpose or object underlying the Act`) AND `the second construction promotes the purpose or object underlying the Act`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Purpose for which extrinsic material is considered` IS ONE OF
    `to confirm that the meaning of the provision is the ordinary meaning conveyed by its text, in its context and in the light of the purpose or object underlying the Act`
    `to determine the meaning of the provision`
    `for some other purpose`

-- Material not forming part of the Act that is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning may be considered to confirm the ordinary meaning,
-- or to determine the meaning when the provision is ambiguous or obscure, or the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or unreasonable.
-- src:739 | (1) In interpreting a provision of an Act, if material not forming part of the Act is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning of the provision, the material may be considered:
-- src:740 | (a) to confirm that the meaning of the provision is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act; or
-- src:741 | (b) to determine the meaning of the provision when:
-- src:742 | (i) the provision is ambiguous or obscure; or
-- src:743 | (ii) the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable.
@ref s 62B(1) (src:739-743)
GIVEN `the material is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `Purpose for which extrinsic material is considered`
      `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62B(1): the material may be considered` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `the material is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning of the provision`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER purpose
         WHEN `to confirm that the meaning of the provision is the ordinary meaning conveyed by its text, in its context and in the light of the purpose or object underlying the Act` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to determine the meaning of the provision` THEN JUST (`the provision is ambiguous or obscure` OR `the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable`)
         WHEN `for some other purpose` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of extrinsic material` IS ONE OF
    `matters not forming part of the Act that are set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer`
    `a report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body laid before the Legislative Assembly`
    `a report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly made to the Assembly`
    `a treaty or other international agreement referred to in the Act`
    `an explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill, or another relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of the Assembly`
    `an explanatory speech or statement given to the Assembly on introducing the Bill`
    `a document declared by the Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of section 62B`
    `relevant material in an official record of debates in the Legislative Assembly`
    `some other material`

-- Without limiting subsection (1), the material that may be considered includes the eight kinds listed.
-- Three of them (the reports of the Royal Commission and the like, the committee report, and the explanatory memorandum) must have come before the provision was enacted.
-- src:744 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the material that may be considered in interpreting a provision of an Act includes the following:
-- src:745 | (a) all matters not forming part of the Act that are set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer;
-- src:746 | (b) any relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body that was laid before the Legislative Assembly before the time when the provision was enacted;
-- src:747 | (c) any relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly that was made to the Legislative Assembly before the time when the provision was enacted;
-- src:748 | (d) any treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act;
-- src:749 | (e) any explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill containing the provision, or any other relevant document, that was laid before, or furnished to the members of the Legislative Assembly by a Minister or other Member before the time when the provision was enacted;
-- src:750 | (f) any explanatory speech or statement given by a Minister or other Member to the Legislative Assembly on introducing the Bill;
-- src:751 | (g) any document (whether or not a document to which a preceding paragraph applies) that is declared by the Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of this section;
-- src:752 | (h) any relevant material in any official record of debates in the Legislative Assembly.
@ref s 62B(2) (src:744-752)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of extrinsic material`
      `it was laid before, made to, or furnished to the Legislative Assembly before the time when the provision was enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62B(2): the material is within the material that may be considered` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `some other material` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body laid before the Legislative Assembly` THEN
        IF `it was laid before, made to, or furnished to the Legislative Assembly before the time when the provision was enacted` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `a report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly made to the Assembly` THEN
        IF `it was laid before, made to, or furnished to the Legislative Assembly before the time when the provision was enacted` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `an explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill, or another relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of the Assembly` THEN
        IF `it was laid before, made to, or furnished to the Legislative Assembly before the time when the provision was enacted` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Where a provision expresses an idea in particular words and a later provision appears to express the same idea in different words to implement a different drafting practice,
-- the ideas must not be taken to be different merely because different words are used.
-- src:754 | (1) Subsection (2) applies if:
-- src:755 | (a) a provision of an Act expresses an idea in particular words; and
-- src:756 | (b) a provision of the Act enacted later appears to express the same idea in different words for the purpose of implementing a different legislative drafting practice.
-- src:757 | (2) The ideas must not be taken to be different merely because different words are used.
@ref s 62C (src:754-757)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act expresses an idea in particular words` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision enacted later appears to express the same idea in different words for the purpose of implementing a different legislative drafting practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason offered is that different words are used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62C: the ideas are taken to be different` MEANS
    IF   `a provision of an Act expresses an idea in particular words`
         AND `a provision enacted later appears to express the same idea in different words for the purpose of implementing a different legislative drafting practice`
         AND `the only reason offered is that different words are used`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- An example in a provision is not exhaustive.
-- src:759 | If a provision of an Act includes an example:
-- src:760 | (a) the example is not exhaustive;
@ref s 62D(a) (src:759-760)
GIVEN `the provision includes an example` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62D(a): the example is exhaustive` MEANS
    IF `the provision includes an example` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- An example does not limit or extend the meaning of the provision.
-- src:759 | If a provision of an Act includes an example:
-- src:760 | (a) the example is not exhaustive;
-- src:761 | (b) the example does not limit or extend the meaning of the provision; and
@ref s 62D(b) (src:759-761)
GIVEN `the provision includes an example` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62D(b): the example limits or extends the meaning of the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision includes an example` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- If an example is inconsistent with the provision, the provision prevails to the extent of the inconsistency.
-- src:759 | If a provision of an Act includes an example:
-- src:760 | (a) the example is not exhaustive;
-- src:761 | (b) the example does not limit or extend the meaning of the provision; and
-- src:762 | (c) if the example is inconsistent with the provision, the provision prevails to the extent of the inconsistency.
@ref s 62D(c) (src:759-762)
GIVEN `the provision includes an example` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the example is inconsistent with the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62D(c): the provision prevails over the example to the extent of the inconsistency` MEANS
    IF `the provision includes an example` AND `the example is inconsistent with the provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- A note at the foot of a provision is not exhaustive and does not limit or extend the meaning of the provision.
-- src:764 | (1) A note at the foot of a provision:
-- src:765 | (a) is not exhaustive; and
-- src:766 | (b) does not limit or extend the meaning of the provision.
@ref s 62E(1) (src:764-766)
GIVEN `the note is at the foot of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62E(1): the note is exhaustive or limits or extends the meaning of the provision` MEANS
    IF `the note is at the foot of a provision` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- If a note at the foot of a provision is inconsistent with the provision, the provision prevails to the extent of the inconsistency.
-- src:767 | (2) If a note at the foot of a provision is inconsistent with the provision, the provision prevails to the extent of the inconsistency.
@ref s 62E(2) (src:767)
GIVEN `the note is at the foot of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note is inconsistent with the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62E(2): the provision prevails over the note to the extent of the inconsistency` MEANS
    IF `the note is at the foot of a provision` AND `the note is inconsistent with the provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
